1
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:05,480
Before... you said you wanted 
to be friends, but...

2
00:00:05,990 --> 00:00:07,700
My feelings for you...

3
00:00:08,590 --> 00:00:10,480
are not just friendship.

4
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:11,750
What?

5
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:22,240
Y-You're right!

6
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:26,100
Even though we're friends now, 
I'm still your mentor.

7
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:27,630
A superior.

8
00:00:28,410 --> 00:00:31,960
So of course we're not just friends... um...

9
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:35,470
Senpai, I...

10
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:39,430
Kamegawa-kun!

11
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:43,560
We want the birthday people 
to do a little closing statement.

12
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:46,000
Is now a bad time?

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,690
No, it's okay.

14
00:00:47,690 --> 00:00:49,400
I'll be right there.

15
00:00:57,780 --> 00:00:59,660
Are you okay, Senpai?

16
00:01:00,130 --> 00:01:01,710
Kannawa-senpai?

17
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:05,200
Senpai? Hey.

18
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:09,000
S-Senpai!

19
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,900
Pull yourself together!

20
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:14,470
I...

21
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:15,700
Huh?

22
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,970
I need booze.

23
00:01:21,030 --> 00:01:24,080
"I Really Thought About It, Ya Know?!"

24
00:01:26,170 --> 00:01:28,730
Now, that...

25
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,430
sounds like a confession.

26
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:37,450
B-But he didn't exactly say that it was.

27
00:01:37,450 --> 00:01:40,060
I feel like I can finally say this now.

28
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:42,970
His feelings for you have 
been obvious for ages now.

29
00:01:42,970 --> 00:01:44,220
They have?

30
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:47,210
Like, "I'm in love with Kannawa-senpai!"

31
00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:48,490
What?!

32
00:01:50,010 --> 00:01:55,260
Kankaiji-senpai and I wished he would 
just hurry up and ask you out.

33
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:02,360
But I think Kamegawa just blurted 
that out today on an impulse.

34
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:06,310
Getting a present from you 
got him all excited.

35
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:13,260
This gift from you makes
 me especially happy.

36
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:20,370
Which is why I think he'll make a 
comeback and properly ask you out.

37
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:21,150
What?

38
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:24,790
Who knows? Maybe he'll call you right now.

39
00:02:33,290 --> 00:02:35,130
It's a toll-free number.

40
00:02:37,230 --> 00:02:39,050
Are you not happy about this?

41
00:02:39,330 --> 00:02:40,010
Huh?

42
00:02:40,010 --> 00:02:42,090
Being asked out by Kamegawa.

43
00:02:42,090 --> 00:02:45,060
It's not that... I just...

44
00:02:49,690 --> 00:02:53,560
AZUSA KANNAWA-SENPAI

45
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:00,760
So? Did you ask her out?

46
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:10,410
No, I didn't...

47
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:13,790
It's more like I planted the idea of it.

48
00:03:14,970 --> 00:03:18,800
Was it because someone 
interrupted in the middle?

49
00:03:20,410 --> 00:03:22,260
No. It was my fault.

50
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:24,100
Well, I suppose.

51
00:03:24,990 --> 00:03:30,230
You were aiming low by suggesting 
 being friends in the first place.

52
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:35,890
Tell me, Kamegawa-kun. What's your type?

53
00:03:35,890 --> 00:03:37,860
M-My type?

54
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:42,510
I like people like Kannawa.

55
00:03:43,410 --> 00:03:46,280
They make me feel competitive or something.

56
00:03:47,410 --> 00:03:48,240
Competitive?

57
00:03:48,850 --> 00:03:51,670
Kind of like how you want to 
climb a wall more the higher it is.

58
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:56,530
But in the end, I couldn't quite 
get along with Kannawa.

59
00:03:56,530 --> 00:03:59,680
What? Really?

60
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:03,120
Let's go outside for a bit.

61
00:04:04,390 --> 00:04:05,380
Sure.

62
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:11,870
Looks like it stopped snowing.

63
00:04:11,870 --> 00:04:12,760
Yeah.

64
00:04:15,270 --> 00:04:20,080
It was only recently that Kannawa 
started talking normally.

65
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:24,860
But a certain someone didn't seem 
to realize that and got all jealous.

66
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:32,080
You know how Kannawa doesn't 
try to make others like her?

67
00:04:33,330 --> 00:04:36,310
That's why she doesn't bother 
getting closer to others.

68
00:04:36,810 --> 00:04:40,700
She doesn't believe that 
anyone could ever like her.

69
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:47,220
Look at all those windows.

70
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:49,450
Each one is lit up.

71
00:04:51,890 --> 00:04:58,400
Inside them, so many people could be living 
wonderful lives that I don't know about.

72
00:05:01,230 --> 00:05:03,730
Since you're under Kannawa's 
direct supervision,

73
00:05:03,730 --> 00:05:06,780
there was no way for her 
to avoid interacting with you.

74
00:05:08,930 --> 00:05:15,320
It was probably a good thing that you 
and Kannawa met as mentor and mentee.

75
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:18,890
Yeah.

76
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:38,020
Th-There's still no way to be sure
that was a confession, anyway.

77
00:05:38,290 --> 00:05:41,000
You're still going on about that?

78
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,440
Weren't you happy that 
Kamegawa asked you out?

79
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:47,040
Or is it that...

80
00:05:47,470 --> 00:05:49,710
you don't want to be involved 
in an office romance?

81
00:05:49,710 --> 00:05:53,160
Or that you're not exactly against it, 
but it's a bit bothersome?

82
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:57,420
No... I-It's...

83
00:05:57,790 --> 00:06:00,500
I-It's not... bothersome.

84
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:01,960
Oh?

85
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,840
Wh-What?

86
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:04,990
Then...

87
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:07,250
if he were to say what he said to you

88
00:06:07,250 --> 00:06:10,930
to another girl, how would you feel?

89
00:06:15,730 --> 00:06:16,980
I'd hate it...

90
00:06:18,190 --> 00:06:19,610
Senpai!

91
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:22,140
Tomorrow's our day off!

92
00:06:22,140 --> 00:06:23,820
Let's drink to our hearts' content tonight!

93
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:26,300
And then we'll have a strategy meeting!

94
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:28,320
S-Strategy meeting?

95
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:29,840
To be honest...

96
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:33,210
I bet you're lacking in 
romantic experience, right?

97
00:06:34,750 --> 00:06:36,220
It's hard to believe.

98
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:40,640
You're super pretty, Senpai. 
You'd be so popular.

99
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:42,370
But that's the good thing about you.

100
00:06:42,370 --> 00:06:43,840
O-Okay...

101
00:06:44,290 --> 00:06:47,210
Which is why I've been thinking.

102
00:06:47,550 --> 00:06:49,720
Uh, yeah?

103
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:52,900
Instead of going out immediately...

104
00:06:52,900 --> 00:06:53,800
Uh-huh...

105
00:07:02,190 --> 00:07:05,730
I don't feel rested at all.

106
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:13,390
In the end, Kamegawa never reached out to me.

107
00:07:15,610 --> 00:07:18,750
Not that I'd know what to say if he did...

108
00:07:19,310 --> 00:07:20,120
<i>No!</i>

109
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:22,750
<i>I've thought this through in my own way!</i>

110
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:26,710
<i>Whether that was a confession or not...</i>

111
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:29,500
<i>I'm mentally prepared for either situation!</i>

112
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:31,090
<i>I'm ready!</i>

113
00:07:31,090 --> 00:07:32,110
<i>Now go!</i>

114
00:07:42,340 --> 00:07:43,810
Good morning.

115
00:07:46,020 --> 00:07:47,470
G...

116
00:07:47,470 --> 00:07:49,820
Gewd myorn... ing...

117
00:07:50,090 --> 00:07:50,970
Later!

118
00:07:52,090 --> 00:07:53,820
Huh? Um...

119
00:08:02,490 --> 00:08:05,040
Can I borrow you for a sec, Kannawa-san?

120
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:05,870
Of course.

121
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:13,620
Kannawa-san seems different, don't you think?

122
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:14,740
Really?

123
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:16,620
Isn't she always like that?

124
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:19,520
I think Kamegawa-kun's 
the one acting different.

125
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:22,180
He seems down. I'm worried.

126
00:08:22,590 --> 00:08:24,560
Hey, you three chatterboxes.

127
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:26,310
Get back to work.

128
00:08:27,190 --> 00:08:28,580
Okay.

129
00:08:28,580 --> 00:08:30,690
Good luck out there.

130
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:38,720
<i>Stare...</i>

131
00:08:43,330 --> 00:08:45,450
<i>Th-This is awkward.</i>

132
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:49,930
<i>I think I took too much damage from 
failing my first encounter with him.</i>

133
00:08:50,580 --> 00:08:51,500
Um...

134
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:54,170
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-What?

135
00:08:54,170 --> 00:08:58,430
Y-Y-Y-Y-You must be worried about 
what happened the other day.

136
00:08:59,430 --> 00:09:01,780
I-I'm so sorry.

137
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:04,600
I said something weird to you 
without thinking it through.

138
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:07,940
You don't need to worry about it right now.

139
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:10,650
O-Okay.

140
00:09:10,650 --> 00:09:12,260
F-For now!

141
00:09:13,090 --> 00:09:15,010
Um...

142
00:09:15,010 --> 00:09:17,580
I'm going to go buy something to drink.

143
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:24,200
Something... weird?

144
00:09:29,010 --> 00:09:30,250
Weird?

145
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:34,640
That was... "weird"?

146
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:38,740
To Kamegawa, it was weird?

147
00:09:38,740 --> 00:09:41,010
As in, somethin' I don't need to worry about?

148
00:09:41,010 --> 00:09:43,870
I even got advice from Hotta about this...

149
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:53,190
Over the weekend, I...

150
00:09:53,490 --> 00:09:56,940
really thought about it, ya know!

151
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:09,530
What am I doing?

152
00:10:17,660 --> 00:10:18,480
Huh?

153
00:10:19,090 --> 00:10:19,960
Huh?!

154
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:49,000
What do ya mean, "weird"?

155
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,380
What do ya mean, "don't worry"?!

156
00:10:53,010 --> 00:10:55,040
Um, Senpai...

157
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:57,140
I'm sorry about before.

158
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:59,380
Um, I also couldn't really...

159
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:00,380
You...

160
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:02,390
You said I was special!

161
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:03,900
That it wasn't just friendship!

162
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:05,880
You kept sayin' stuff that made no sense!

163
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:10,270
I lost sleep this weekend 'cuz I couldn't 
stop thinkin' 'bout what ya said!

164
00:11:10,270 --> 00:11:12,680
"Don't worry about it"?

165
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:14,400
Of course I'm gonna worry!

166
00:11:14,830 --> 00:11:16,360
Of course I'll worry about it!

167
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:21,360
So I...

168
00:11:23,210 --> 00:11:25,860
just kept thinkin' 'bout ya!

169
00:11:25,860 --> 00:11:27,500
I can't even work.

170
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:30,120
And it's affecting my daily life!

171
00:11:30,510 --> 00:11:33,130
So I wanna do somethin' 'bout this!

172
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:43,820
Um...

173
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:46,100
I...

174
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:46,970
So...

175
00:11:46,970 --> 00:11:48,680
Y-Yes, ma'am!

176
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:51,750
I've thought it through these last two days!

177
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:52,600
Yes, ma'am!

178
00:11:54,950 --> 00:11:56,480
Three months!

179
00:11:58,180 --> 00:12:00,830
A three-month trial!

180
00:12:00,830 --> 00:12:02,740
T-Trial?

181
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:06,870
I'm sayin' that I'll give ya 
my time for three months.

182
00:12:10,810 --> 00:12:11,730
What do you think?

183
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:13,120
You can't pass this up.

184
00:12:14,030 --> 00:12:17,580
What? Um... this conversation 
took quite a turn, and...

185
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:20,840
I can't keep up.

186
00:12:21,470 --> 00:12:23,010
Don't you want it?

187
00:12:23,010 --> 00:12:24,890
I-I do!

188
00:12:24,890 --> 00:12:25,950
All right!

189
00:12:25,950 --> 00:12:27,390
Then it's decided!

190
00:12:27,690 --> 00:12:28,840
Hold on!

191
00:12:29,310 --> 00:12:30,990
Before we talk about that...

192
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:34,910
I... have something I need to tell y—

193
00:12:36,290 --> 00:12:37,340
Nope!

194
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:38,270
Huh?!

195
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:43,940
I've used up my energy for the day!

196
00:12:45,940 --> 00:12:47,530
I'm going home!

197
00:12:48,550 --> 00:12:49,660
Yes, ma'am...

198
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:31,460
Kannawa-senpai!

199
00:13:32,510 --> 00:13:34,480
I was so moved!

200
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,540
You were actually able to say it!

201
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:40,090
Yeah. You gave us quite the show.

202
00:13:40,090 --> 00:13:42,840
It was... It was...

203
00:13:43,210 --> 00:13:47,380
It was... completely one-sided...

204
00:13:47,380 --> 00:13:48,920
It's okay!

205
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:52,250
I'm sure Kamegawa's doing 
a little dance right now!

206
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:57,180
I heard the two of you had a strategy meeting 
and decided on the three-month trial?

207
00:13:57,180 --> 00:13:58,680
Y-Yeah.

208
00:13:58,680 --> 00:14:01,060
When we were drinking the other day...

209
00:14:01,580 --> 00:14:05,790
The relationship between the two of you 
started as mentor and mentee,

210
00:14:05,790 --> 00:14:08,050
so you skipped through a lot of stuff.

211
00:14:08,050 --> 00:14:09,660
Like going on dates.

212
00:14:09,660 --> 00:14:10,910
Da—

213
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:14,120
Going out somewhere together, 
eating somewhere...

214
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:17,230
I think you should start by giving those a try!

215
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,900
Give them a try?

216
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:23,550
In other words, a dating period!

217
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:25,920
Dating?

218
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:31,200
It's the trial period to get to know each 
other before officially becoming a couple.

219
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:32,580
Oh, yeah!

220
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:34,690
That's exactly it!

221
00:14:34,690 --> 00:14:36,350
Th-Then...

222
00:14:36,670 --> 00:14:40,560
is there something I should be doing 
during the dating period?

223
00:14:40,990 --> 00:14:43,320
Like, any specific places we should go?

224
00:14:44,030 --> 00:14:45,550
Hmm...

225
00:14:46,780 --> 00:14:51,280
First, you should drop the idea that 
there's something specific you need to do.

226
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:52,120
Huh?

227
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:56,080
You could end up being 
too formal because of that.

228
00:14:56,650 --> 00:14:58,350
Just let things happen naturally.

229
00:14:58,660 --> 00:15:00,830
Wh-What do you mean, "naturally"?

230
00:15:00,830 --> 00:15:03,290
You're already being too 
self-conscious, Senpai!

231
00:15:03,750 --> 00:15:06,250
Enjoy your dating period.

232
00:15:07,250 --> 00:15:08,300
Okay.

233
00:15:08,300 --> 00:15:10,420
Remember, Senpai, act natural.

234
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:12,050
Extra natural!

235
00:15:12,050 --> 00:15:13,750
Y-Yeah!

236
00:15:29,150 --> 00:15:34,120
Which of these did Kamegawa 
have the best reaction to?

237
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:37,120
<i>Oh.</i>

238
00:15:37,450 --> 00:15:38,540
<i>But...</i>

239
00:15:40,270 --> 00:15:42,290
<i>"They all look good," he said.</i>

240
00:15:42,290 --> 00:15:44,170
<i>He complimented me on all of them.</i>

241
00:15:51,390 --> 00:15:52,260
Okay!

242
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:15,700
<i>I'm so nervous that I ended up 
arrivin' super early.</i>

243
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:30,150
Senpai!

244
00:16:32,820 --> 00:16:34,220
Why're you here?

245
00:16:34,220 --> 00:16:35,310
Huh?

246
00:16:35,310 --> 00:16:36,920
Oh, I mean...

247
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:40,260
I'm one to talk, 
but you're thirty minutes early.

248
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:41,700
That's too much.

249
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:44,440
Yeah... I got nervous.

250
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:48,140
We're just going to eat ramen.

251
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:50,660
What's there to be nervous about?

252
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:54,230
B-But isn't this... a date?

253
00:16:55,410 --> 00:16:57,150
I-It's a trial!

254
00:16:57,150 --> 00:16:58,410
A trial date.

255
00:16:58,870 --> 00:17:01,870
Right. It's a trial date.

256
00:17:04,120 --> 00:17:06,500
The tree is so pretty!

257
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:08,380
Let's take a closer look at it together.

258
00:17:10,390 --> 00:17:11,220
Yeah.

259
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:16,500
Have you decided on the restaurant?

260
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:17,380
Oh.

261
00:17:18,030 --> 00:17:22,580
I-I saw on TV a while ago that 
there's this good place near here.

262
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:25,140
I only remember that it's in this area.

263
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:29,450
Oh, sorry.

264
00:17:29,450 --> 00:17:31,630
I kind of figured this would happen,

265
00:17:31,630 --> 00:17:33,370
so I did some research on my end.

266
00:17:33,370 --> 00:17:36,430
Wh-What do you mean, you "kind of figured"?!

267
00:17:36,830 --> 00:17:38,720
S-Sorry.

268
00:17:42,210 --> 00:17:44,160
So? Where is it?

269
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,810
Oh, um...

270
00:17:45,810 --> 00:17:48,670
A famous place around here would be...

271
00:17:48,670 --> 00:17:49,880
Maybe this one?

272
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,550
Oh! That! That's the one!

273
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:55,920
It looks good.

274
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:57,680
I'm so glad.

275
00:17:57,680 --> 00:17:59,340
Thanks, Kamegawa.

276
00:17:59,340 --> 00:18:01,430
You're welcome.

277
00:18:01,430 --> 00:18:04,670
Speaking of ramen, do you...

278
00:18:07,370 --> 00:18:08,670
like...

279
00:18:17,810 --> 00:18:19,870
Yes, I do.

280
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:23,530
That's good.

281
00:18:25,190 --> 00:18:27,320
Sorry for hitting you.

282
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:29,790
It's all right.

283
00:18:31,170 --> 00:18:32,290
Okay.

284
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:39,780
You've got bedhead.

285
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:40,780
Like, a lot.

286
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:43,050
What? Where?

287
00:18:44,310 --> 00:18:45,310
Just kiddin'.

288
00:18:47,010 --> 00:18:48,330
Well, you...

289
00:18:48,330 --> 00:18:49,130
Hmm?

290
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:50,940
Hmm...

291
00:18:54,850 --> 00:18:56,440
You're cute.

292
00:18:57,190 --> 00:18:57,900
Wha—

293
00:18:58,250 --> 00:19:01,020
What made the conversation
 take that turn?!

294
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:01,930
No, uh...

295
00:19:01,930 --> 00:19:03,910
I was going for a comeback,

296
00:19:04,350 --> 00:19:07,830
but I couldn't think of anything 
negative about you.

297
00:19:07,830 --> 00:19:09,360
Sorry.

298
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:12,500
It's rude to say that to your superior.

299
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:13,330
But...

300
00:19:15,530 --> 00:19:19,300
you're not here with me as my superior today.

301
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:23,270
W-Well... about that...

302
00:19:23,890 --> 00:19:28,160
You're here to give me three months 
of your time... Kannawa-san.

303
00:19:36,060 --> 00:19:40,580
I still don't understand what 
you meant when you said

304
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:43,380
that I was special to you.

305
00:19:43,380 --> 00:19:45,100
I can't even imagine it.

306
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:50,760
Which is why I want to learn much more 
about you over the next three months.

307
00:19:51,390 --> 00:19:53,830
And I want you to learn more about me.

308
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:55,790
And...

309
00:19:55,790 --> 00:20:00,550
I want to know what that 
special thing between us is.

310
00:20:02,510 --> 00:20:03,450
Sure.

311
00:20:09,670 --> 00:20:11,910
I-Is this okay?

312
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:15,980
Only until we get to the restaurant.

313
00:20:16,790 --> 00:20:17,750
Okay.

314
00:20:25,570 --> 00:20:27,580
L-Let's go!

315
00:20:27,580 --> 00:20:28,780
Which way?

316
00:20:29,530 --> 00:20:30,750
That way.

317
00:20:30,750 --> 00:20:32,580
Oh, that way!

318
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:33,980
Okay, let's go!

319
00:22:18,010 --> 00:22:20,440
Looks like we can go in shortly.

320
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:21,280
Yeah.

321
00:22:21,750 --> 00:22:24,020
Do you already know what you're getting?

322
00:22:24,020 --> 00:22:25,560
Nope!

323
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:26,730
Here's the menu.

324
00:22:26,730 --> 00:22:28,940
Oh, thanks. That helps.

325
00:22:29,740 --> 00:22:32,170
Next in line. Kamegawa-sama!

326
00:22:32,170 --> 00:22:33,210
Yesh!

327
00:22:33,210 --> 00:22:35,290
Oh, wait, that's not me.

328
00:22:35,290 --> 00:22:36,910
Oh, but...

329
00:22:36,910 --> 00:22:38,780
We're Kamegawa.

330
00:22:39,250 --> 00:22:40,310
Come on in.

331
00:22:46,570 --> 00:22:48,880
So good.

332
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:50,540
It's delicious.

333
00:22:50,540 --> 00:22:52,580
It hits the spot.

334
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:54,510
Want to try some of mine?

335
00:22:54,510 --> 00:22:57,240
Can I? Thank you.

336
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:11,440
So? Do you like it?

337
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:19,760
It's delicious! I can see why it's 
a popular spot. Right, Senpai?

338
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:22,320
Yes. Ah, um...

339
00:23:22,320 --> 00:23:24,750
Let's finish before the noodles get soggy.

340
00:23:24,750 --> 00:23:26,540
Y-You're right.

341
00:23:30,610 --> 00:23:33,550
Let's go to lots more places from now on.

342
00:23:34,670 --> 00:23:35,510
Yeah.

